  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fact-finding mission Public Finance Management (Algeria, Egypt, Morocco and Tunisia)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building on previous experience in the Shiraka Training Programme, the overall and long-term target is to improve Public Finance Management in the four selected countries by setting-up a multi-annual technical assistance programme. These four countries all have embarked on ambitious public financial management reforms and are looking for foreign expertise to assist them with their implementation tailored towards their needs. The envisioned assistance from the Netherlands Ministry of Finance (NL MoF) will be more targeted and comprehensive than is currently possible under the Shiraka Training Programme. It will be based on availability and capacity of expertise of the NL MoF in conjunction with the requested needs for technical assistance. The future assistance programme will most likely target the areas in which the National Academy can provide expertise, i.e. policy-based fiscal strategy and budgeting, budget reliability, predictability and control in budget execution, transparency of public finances, policy evaluation and audit.</narrative>
  </description>
